The diagram shows two hyperbolas, $C_1$ and $C_2$, on the Cartesian plane.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-7, xmax=7, ymin=-7, ymax=7, samples=200, clip=false, restrict y to domain=-7.5:7.5, unbounded coords=jump, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick={-6,-4,-2,2,4,6}, ytick={-6,-4,-2,2,4,6}]
\addplot[dashed, gray, thick] coordinates {(0,-6.5) (0,6.5)};
\addplot[dashed, gray, thick] coordinates {(-6.5,0) (6.5,0)};
\node[gray] at (axis cs:-4.5,6.0) {$x=0$};
\node[gray] at (axis cs:4.2,-1.6) {$y=0$};
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=1.15:6.5] {7/x};
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-6.5:-1.15] {7/x};
\addplot[thick, red, <->, domain=0.35:6.5] {2/x};
\addplot[thick, red, <->, domain=-6.5:-0.35] {2/x};
\node[above right, blue] at (axis cs:3.5,2) {$C_1$};
\node[below left, red] at (axis cs:2,1) {$C_2$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which statement correctly compares curve $C_1$ to curve $C_2$?
